license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Ophamin is a Python framework that turns experiments into signed
  empirical proof records. Every measurement is bound to its
  pre-registered falsifiable claim, to a byte-equal data corpus, to a
  versioned substrate-under-test, and to a tamper-evident HMAC-SHA256
  signature; the verdict (VALIDATED / REFUTED / INCONCLUSIVE) is
  computed mechanically from the claim's threshold rather than chosen
  by the experimenter. The signed-record wire format is normatively
  specified and verified byte-for-byte by read + write ports in Rust
  (`crates/ophamin-proof`) and JavaScript / TypeScript
  (`packages/ophamin-proof-js`); the round-trip is symmetric — any
  port emits, any port verifies. Five interop layers wrap the same
  shared implementations: cross-language wire-format
  (Rust + JS read + write), an MCP server (`ophamin mcp serve`) for
  agent-callable access (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, Cline),
  an HTTP REST API (`ophamin http serve`) for service-style consumers,
  a CloudEvents 1.0 wrapper for event-stream interop, and OpenTelemetry
  instrumentation (spans + metrics) for production observability. The
  measurement-machinery tier includes seven cross-framework validation
  scenarios (Bayesian PyMC↔NumPyro, Wilson CI scipy↔statsmodels,
  Spearman scipy↔pingouin, Pearson scipy↔numpy↔pingouin, Welch's t-test
  scipy↔statsmodels↔pingouin, one-way ANOVA three-way, Mann-Whitney U
  scipy↔pingouin) — each a signed VALIDATED proof at floating-point
  agreement levels.
